comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T22:37:34.363Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: hybrid expected-error diagnostics search plus complete PmCliErrorContext keyword search found existing host-specific contracts but no open extension-owned payload slot; checked live open and in-progress lists; related active provenance work retains its current scope."
  "2026-11-01T21:06:26.813Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation (branch fix/refusal-contract-precision):\n\n- Contract: PmCliErrorContext gains an optional details slot typed PmCliErrorDetails (plain JSON: null, booleans, finite numbers, well-formed strings, arrays, plain objects). New core module src/core/shared/error-details.ts admits a value, returns a detached copy, and renders it whole within PM_CLI_ERROR_DETAILS_LIMITS (max_bytes 4096 of compact UTF-8 JSON, max_depth 8). Anything larger or malformed is replaced by a details_omitted receipt { reason, path?, byte_length?, byte_limit }. Partial structures are never emitted.\n- SDK: createPmCliExpectedError validates details at construction and throws a TypeError naming the reason and path (unsupported_value, non_finite_number, malformed_unicode, reserved_key for __proto__, depth_limit, not_plain_object). Size is data-dependent, so it is bounded at render time, not refused. Exports from sdk and sdk/runtime: PM_CLI_ERROR_DETAILS_LIMITS, isPmCliErrorDetails, PmCliErrorDetails, PmCliErrorDetailValue, PmCliErrorDetailsOmission, PmCliErrorDetailsRejection.\n- CLI: --json errors carry details or details_omitted (kept by --lean). Text output renders an indented TOON \"Details:\" block, which is the first collection the bounded text ladder drops. The telemetry classification is built without details.\n- MCP: errorContent and writeError now recognize separately bundled expected errors by shape (they previously forwarded context only for instanceof PmCliError) and bound details the same way.\n- Sentry: captured faults strip details from error_context, and beforeSend scrubs details from error-data contexts and extras.\n\nProof: tests/unit/core/shared/error-details.spec.ts (17 cases), error-guidance, MCP, Sentry helper/instrument and SDK index specs. tests/integration/telemetry/extension-error-provenance.spec.ts runs the built CLI under Node and Bun against real local OTLP and Sentry collectors: the probe extension's separately bundled refusal carries a marked details payload, the JSON refusal returns it whole, the text refusal renders the Details block, and the marker never appears in collected events, logs or telemetry.\n\nProducer adoption (pm-changelog selection_report) belongs in the pm-changelog repository once a pm-cli release ships this slot. Filed there as the follow-up after merge.\n"
